            <ArticleTitle>Laparoscopic repair of an intrapericardial diaphragmatic hernia.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>332-3</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.athoracsur.2013.04.127</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">S0003-4975(13)01106-5</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>An isolated intrapericardial diaphragmatic hernia is very rare. Only 15 cases have been reported, 2 of which are in adults. The defect in the anterior diaphragm allows abdominal contents to enter the pericardial cavity. We report the 16th case--the third in an adult--and its laparoscopic repair.</AbstractText>
